+# Combined Eager and Compiled Direct-Arena MRE
+
+This temporary branch combines the independently reviewed eager table-aware
+prototype at `b025c4a7b31f9f225ed73024c86d35ffd95c6fdd` with the compiled
+Direct-Arena series through
+`7cff626d304f85465b083c150d5e8b0f189b43c5`. It is an integration MRE, not an
+authoritative pyAmpliCol or recurrence checkout.
+
+The two execution contracts remain separate:
+
+- eager table callables execute a row-outer/point-inner schedule with explicit
+  plane/scalar parameter bindings, multiple complex outputs, and ordered
+  whole-output attachment fanout;
+- compiled callables use `Initialize + Identity` O3 applications with
+  factor-free multiple-output stores and source-first v3 storage.
+
+Exact-factor direct applications retain their O2 requirement and recurrence
+destination semantics. Compiled identity applications require O3. The eager
+table boundary rejects complete-range same-row input/output and destination
+collisions while permitting ordered cross-row producer/consumer,
+expired-input, and destination-reuse aliases. Scalar, factor, table, and
+descriptor-catalog buffers remain globally protected. Warmed checked and
+unchecked calls allocate zero. The eager table fixture remains the pinned
+360-byte built-in-SM recurrence-canary payload with SHA-256
+`558b681aab77670552237c3ca544cc618a23851586c244e873188921b48d73ab`;
+this wording does not claim that the still-evolving recurrence branch is
+accepted or source-frozen.
+
+Conflict resolution deliberately retained both portable-source transformation
+tests and both allocation regressions. The eager table allocation probe is the
+single test global allocator and is reused by compiled plane-call tests.
+The pinned eager payload stays O3 for table execution. An untouched O3 dense
+evaluation establishes both complex outputs bit-for-bit through complete
+four-component attachments and two-way fanout. The separate O2 exact-factor
+DirectApplication oracle still lowers the retained first-output MIR to
+validate factor, operation, and fanout ordering.
+`DIRECT_APPLICATION_STORAGE_ABI` remains the sole current writer identity,
+`symjit-direct-application-storage-v3`. A narrow read-only compatibility path
+accepts accepted recurrence exact-factor O2 v1 payloads, identified separately
+by `DIRECT_APPLICATION_LEGACY_V1_STORAGE_ABI`; their already-lowered callable
+is fully revalidated before use and cannot be reserialized as v3. V2 remains
+unsupported.
+
+The eager side now also has a separate bounded source-first descriptor codec.
+It serializes only little-endian fixed-width metadata, never executable bytes
+or pointers, and validates loaded-source counts before bounded allocation.
+
+This MRE proves that both proposed SymJIT ABI extensions coexist. It does not
+provide pyAmpliCol artifact wiring, x86-64 table callable generation, or
+end-to-end performance evidence; those remain cutover gates in the feature
+worktree. Eager descriptors and validation are architecture-neutral, but
+`DirectTableApplication::seal` reports the x86 callable gap explicitly.
+
+## Validation
+
+On the AArch64 MRE host, strict all-target Clippy passes, and both the debug and
+optimized library suites pass 43/43. Both integration suites pass 4/4. All
+build/test commands are guarded by the 30 GiB watchdog; the largest observed
+peak in the hardened debug/release validation is 0.656 GiB RSS.
+
+The former optimized-integration SIGSEGVs in
+`compressed_storage_v3_roundtrip_is_exact_and_stable` and
+`compressed_vector_matches_expanded` were independently traced to the test
+fixture compiling state-backed inputs while invoking the parameter-backed
+`Application::evaluate` entry point. The integrated fix from
+`2fe9f777c10340e9ae80a0bccd04da7487e27da9` compiles those inputs as
+parameters and adds non-vacuity assertions; both debug and optimized
+integration suites now pass 4/4. `RELEASE_SIGSEGV_DIAGNOSIS.md` preserves the
+root-cause and machine-code evidence.
