+# Compiled O3 Direct-Arena MRE
+
+This additive prototype extends the existing portable Direct-Arena
+application with an identity output scale orthogonal to the existing
+destination operation. Compiled applications use `Initialize + Identity`;
+the two-bit operation encoding remains unchanged.
+
+The compiled output contract:
+
+- accepts portable Native Symbolica complex O3 MIR;
+- preserves compressed funclet calls and labels;
+- maps every source parameter to a point-contiguous input plane;
+- writes multiple outputs to distinct persistent planes;
+- reserves no exact-factor scalar slots;
+- performs no factor multiplication at the output boundary; and
+- rejects input/output, scalar/output, and output/output aliasing across full
+  declared ranges in the checked call.
+
+The recurrence O2 operations retain their existing exact-factor and aliased
+destination contracts. Direct-application storage is intentionally bumped to
+v3; no v1/v2 reader is retained. Version 3 stores the portable source application
+before source-sized direct metadata, then validates and re-lowers at load time.
+Encoded metadata counts must match the loaded source before any metadata vector
+is reserved. It never
+serializes the already-complexified Direct-Arena MIR as though it were a source
+application.
+
+The focused tests compare the direct plane result bitwise with the ordinary
+dense O3 application for 1, 2, 3, 127, 128, and 129 points. They also prove
+that both source and lowered machine code contain an out-of-line compressed
+funclet call, identity stores preserve signed zero/subnormal/NaN payload bits,
+and checked calls reject exact and partial overlap across complete declared
+plane ranges, including future input/scalar tiles and output/output overlap.
+Storage tests exercise valid Identity/O3 round trips, shared source loading,
+legacy and malformed v2 rejection, nonportable source configuration rejection,
+and panic containment. Warmed checked and unchecked plane calls allocate zero.
+
+The prototype intentionally does not add a table-row outer loop or claim an
+end-to-end speedup. Its interface contains only borrowed plane descriptors and
+therefore has no packet/gather/scatter buffer path, but it does not claim
+end-to-end pyAmpliCol traffic measurements. It isolates the higher-risk O3,
+factor-free, multiple-output, odd-tail ABI required before measuring a real
+compiled stage in pyAmpliCol.
