+# Optimized integration-test SIGSEGV diagnosis
+
+## Scope
+
+This diagnosis applies to combined Direct-Arena MRE commit
+`e1c84e9d2e35569f253020347848d0a5bb134309`. The original optimized
+reproducer was:
+
+```text
+cargo test --release --test arm_compress \
+  compressed_storage_v3_roundtrip_is_exact_and_stable -- --exact --nocapture
+```
+
+It exited with `SIGSEGV` after every assertion in the test body had completed.
+The first guarded build/reproducer peaked at 1.524 GiB RSS.
+
+## Root cause
+
+The `arm_compress` fixture compiled `x`, `y`, and `z` as application *states*
+using `Compiler::compile`, then called `Application::evaluate(args, outs)`.
+That generic entry point passes `outs` as the machine-code memory pointer,
+passes a null indirect-state view, and passes `args` as the parameter pointer.
+It is therefore valid for the parameter-backed evaluator shape used by
+prepared Symbolica applications, not for this state-backed fixture.
+
+The invalid fixture produced an application with six scalar state components,
+two scalar output components, and no parameters. In the emitted AArch64 SIMD
+function:
+
+```text
+0x20   mov x19, x0
+0x34   b.eq 0x88
+0x94   ldp q6, q7, [x19]
+0x98   ldp q16, q17, [x19, #0x20]
+0xc0   ldp q20, q21, [x19, #0x40]
+...
+0xcb0  stp q18, q19, [x19, #0x60]
+```
+
+`x0`/`x19` is the start of the caller's one-element
+`Complex<f64x2>` output, which is only 32 bytes. The JIT reads the nonexistent
+state region through that pointer and stores the result at byte offset 96,
+outside the output. Both compared output arrays normally remained zero, so
+the debug assertion was also vacuous. Optimized stack placement made the
+latent overwrite corrupt live test-harness state and crash after the body
+returned.
+
+## Why this predates the Direct-Arena work
+
+`tests/arm_compress.rs`, `rust/applet.rs`, and `rust/compiler.rs` are byte-for-
+byte unchanged between the imported baseline `575dfdbaa0742160d341d158811079592d359c45`
+and `e1c84e9`. The only changes in the nearby ordinary AArch64 path are field
+visibility and a precomplexified-MIR branch that this fixture does not use.
+The current `rust/applet.rs` also has the same SHA-256
+`65212e6e0f1e96a01a90045709549e0e6cdc0bf2b93e169703373f38b1361438`
+as the locally retained published SymJIT 2.18.9 source.
+
+Neither Direct-Arena ABI invokes this generic state-backed `evaluate` shape.
+`DirectApplication` and `DirectTableApplication` lower and call their own
+validated plane/view entry points. pyAmpliCol's ordinary prepared evaluator
+loader separately requires zero states before sealing an application.
+Consequently this crash does not identify a Direct-Arena kernel, storage, or
+production-call defect.
+
+## Fix and regression coverage
+
+The fixture now compiles its three arguments as parameters with
+`compile_params(&[], outputs, params)`, matching the entry point it exercises.
+It asserts the resulting zero-state/six-parameter/two-output shape and asserts
+that scalar and SIMD results are nonzero, preventing the former out-of-bounds,
+zero-equals-zero test from returning unnoticed.
+
+Both eager table-aware and compiled Direct-Arena contracts remain unchanged.
